<title>SOUTH AFRICA: SAFRICA INDUSTRIAL DEVELOPMENT CORP NAMES NEW HEAD.</title>
<headline>SAFRICA INDUSTRIAL DEVELOPMENT CORP NAMES NEW HEAD.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The South African government said on Wednesday it had appointed Khaya Ngqula as the new chief executive officer of the state-run Industrial Development Corporation (IDC) investment vehicle.</p>
<p>&quot;The (IDC) board has been exhaustive in ensuring the appointment of a person who can lead the IDC from strength strength in the challenging new economic situation,&quot; trade and industry minister Alec Erwin said in a statement.</p>
<p>&quot;The government regards the IDC as a key institution in the development of our economy,&quot; he added.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
